Origin: local fix (same class of bug as upstream MR 27)
Subject: Require GTK 3 in util.lib so the CLI does not load GTK 4

ocrfeeder-cli imports ocrfeeder.util.lib before ocrfeeder.studio.studioBuilder.
The latter calls gi.require_version('Gtk', '3.0'), but lib.py imports
gi.repository.Gtk without a version, so on systems where GTK 4 is also
installed PyGObject loads GTK 4 and Gtk.IconSize.SMALL_TOOLBAR no longer
exists. The GUI is unaffected because it requires the version first.

 src/ocrfeeder/util/lib.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ocrfeeder/util/lib.py
+++ b/src/ocrfeeder/util/lib.py
@@ -27,4 +27,6 @@
 import xml.etree.ElementTree as etree
 
 import sane
+import gi
+gi.require_version('Gtk', '3.0')
 from gi.repository import Gtk
